concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-10-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "270(3) 8  Slavery-like offences—aggravated offences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-270-10-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If, on a trial for an aggravated offence, the trier of fact is not satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence, but is otherwise satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the corresponding slavery-like offence, it may find the defendant not guilty of the aggravated offence, but guilty of the corresponding slavery-like offence." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If, on a trial for an aggravated offence, the trier of fact is not satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence, but is otherwise satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the corresponding slavery-like offence, it may find the defendant not guilty of the aggravated offence, but guilty of the corresponding slavery-like offence."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "54fd041eebc186009aa784ce5375b6a1cff248929ced53465efe00ac05f622e0" ;
