    values:originalText "(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the trier of fact is not satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence, but is satisfied that the defendant is guilty of an offence against section 271.7F, it may find the defendant not guilty of the aggravated offence, but guilty of an offence against that section." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-10-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "271(3) 7G  Harbouring a victim—aggravated offence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-271-10-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded procedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence against section 271.7F. Note: Section 271.7F provides for the offence of harbouring a victim." ;
