doc:sch-1-sec-271-15 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "271 11A  Offences against Division 271—relevant evidence" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of proceedings for an offence against this Division, the trier of fact may have regard to any of the matters covered by subsection (2) in determining whether, in relation to a person (the alleged victim) against whom the offence is alleged to have been committed:  (a) in the case of an offence against Subdivision B or BB—the alleged victim has been coerced, threatened or deceived; or  (b) in the case of an offence against Subdivision BA—the alleged victim, or the alleged victim’s guardian, has consented to the removal of an organ of the alleged victim; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006  Criminal Code amendments  Schedule 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act" ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2013 No. 6, 2013            23"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-2013-10 ;
    values:originalText "(c) in the case of an offence against Subdivision C—another person has caused the alleged victim to enter into debt bondage.  (2) The following matters are covered by this subsection:  (a) the economic relationship between the alleged victim and the alleged offender;  (b) the terms of any written or oral contract or agreement between the alleged victim and the alleged offender;  (c) the personal circumstances of the alleged victim, including but not limited to:  (i) whether he or she is entitled to be in Australia under the Migration Act 1958; and  (ii) his or her ability to speak, write and understand English or another language; and  (iii) the extent of his or her social and physical dependence on the alleged offender.  (3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to the consent of an alleged victim’s guardian to the removal of an organ of the alleged victim, a reference in subsection (2) to the alleged victim is taken to include a reference to the alleged victim’s guardian.  (4) Subsection (1) does not:  (a) prevent the leading of any other evidence in the relevant proceedings; or  (b) limit the manner in which evidence may be given or the admissibility of evidence." ;
    skos:definition "(c) in the case of an offence against Subdivision C—another person has caused the alleged victim to enter into debt bondage.  (2) The following matters are covered by this subsection:  (a) the economic relationship between the alleged victim and the alleged offender;  (b) the terms of any written or oral contract or agreement between the alleged victim and the alleged offender;  (c) the personal circumstances of the alleged victim, including but not limited to:  (i) whether he or she is entitled to be in Australia under the Migration Act 1958; and  (ii) his or her ability to speak, write and understand English or another language; and  (iii) the extent of his or her social and physical dependence on the alleged offender.  (3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to the consent of an alleged victim’s guardian to the removal of an organ of the alleged victim, a reference in subsection (2) to the alleged victim is taken to include a reference to the alleged victim’s guardian.  (4) Subsection (1) does not:  (a) prevent the leading of any other evidence in the relevant proceedings; or  (b) limit the manner in which evidence may be given or the admissibility of evidence."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1c79b188fe2a22812b2c8fff1627c645aeaf226cff18208ce1f1a1c8aaa81f1c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "27"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2013a00006.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2013a00006.pdf, p.27" .
